          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Economic Policies and Stability</strong><br>\nDuring his presidency, Mubarak implemented economic reforms to encourage foreign investment and privatization. His policies aimed at achieving stability led to economic growth, but also criticism over issues of inequality and corruption.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Regional and International Relations</strong><br>\nMubarak played a significant role in regional politics, mediating conflicts and maintaining Egypt's position as a leading Arab state. His leadership saw Egypt's active involvement in peacekeeping initiatives and negotiations in the Middle East.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Domestic Policies and Emergency Law</strong><br>\nMubarak's tenure was marked by a stringent stance on security and the imposition of an emergency law, which expanded police powers, suspended constitutional rights, and legalized censorship.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
