            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Protests and Resignation</strong><br>\nIn January 2011, massive protests erupted against Mubarak's rule, part of the Arab Spring movement. After weeks of protests, Mubarak resigned on February 11, 2011, ending his nearly 30-year presidency.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Trial and Later Life</strong><br>\nFollowing his resignation, Mubarak was put on trial on various charges, including corruption and the killing of protestors. After a protracted legal process, he was released in 2017 and lived a relatively secluded life until his death in 2020.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hosni Mubarak's Legacy</strong><br>\nMubarak's legacy is a complex one, marked by a tenure of stability and growth for Egypt but also by authoritarian rule, corruption, and resistance to political change. His presidency shaped modern Egypt in profound ways.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
